  "summary": "I am a Senior Software Engineer with over 6 years of experience at Lockheed Martin, specializing in high-stakes system integration, secure network infrastructure, and scalable deployments. Today, my primary focus is bridging the gap between mission-critical systems engineering and advanced Artificial Intelligence.\nI don't just work with ML models; I architect the autonomous ecosystems they operate in. Recently, I built and launched The Tribunal (thetribunal.ai)—a multi-agent consensus framework designed for high-stakes decision-making under uncertainty. By orchestrating specialized LLMs into hierarchical layers and engineering a recursive continuous learning pipeline, I develop systems where AI acts, evaluates, and reaches verifiable consensus reliably at scale.\nWhat I bring to the table:\n► Agentic Architecture & AI: Designing multi-agent consensus systems, deterministic LLM orchestration, and efficient fine-tuning pipelines (LoRA/GGUF) using PyTorch and Transformer architectures. ► ML Infrastructure & Compute: Optimizing hybrid cloud and edge inference, hardware acceleration (CUDA/ROCm), and configuring KVM virtualization for heavy GPU workloads. ► Enterprise Systems Engineering: Proven track record of migrating CI/CD to containerized deployments (Podman/Buildah) and deep multi-language development (Python, C, Rust) in strictly regulated environments.\nI thrive on solving complex architectural bottlenecks—whether that means optimizing a local neural network to run efficiently on edge hardware or designing strict capital and risk guardrails for autonomous, tool-calling agents.\nLet’s connect if you are building the future of ML infrastructure, agentic orchestration, or autonomous multi-agent systems.",
